`, `allergy`, `Hypertension`, `hypertension`, `prescription adjustment`, `emergency dispensation`, `medical dispensation`\n\n### Gaps in `rev-001` you should know about before relying on it\n- **Span-priority ordering / overlap resolution:** there is **no** dedicated `span_priority` or `overlap_resolution` block in this revision. The only ordering signal is the per-classifier integer `priority` (1 = highest … 5 = lowest), with ties clustered at priority 2 and priority 3. Tie-breaking, longest-match vs. leftmost-match, containment handling, and cross-category (PII vs. PHI) precedence are **undefined** in `rev-001`. Any pipeline behavior on those points is an implementation choice, not a pinned rule.\n- **Heuristics:** `CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001` is typed `dictionary_and_heuristic`, but only its `terms` list is materialized — no explicit heuristic rules, proximity windows, or context conditions are defined.\n- **Declared-but-unimplemented types:** `NATIONAL_ID`, `CVV`, `PATIENT_ID`, `MEDICAL_CASE_REF`, `CLINICAL_NOTE`, and `CONDITION`/`PRESCRIPTION`/`ALLERGY` as discrete classifiers have no dedicated classifier; they are only reachable via broader patterns or the term list.\n- **False-positive risk at pin time:** `CLS-PII-PASSPORT-001` (`[A-Z]\\d{8,9}`) and `CLS-PII-DL-001` overlap heavily with generic alphanumeric tokens, and `\\b\\d{3}-\\d{2}-\\d{4}\\b` SSN has no checksum/range validation.\n\nAny change to these items requires a new revision; I cannot amend `rev-001` in place.\n\n```json\n{\n  "Name": "Governed system of record — Master Data Classifiers ruleset",\n  "Inquiry": "Return the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset in strict read-only mode: all enabled PII/PHI categories, regex patterns, NER entity types, dictionary term lists, heuristics, confidence thresholds, and classifier_id values, plus span-priority ordering and overlap resolution rules.",\n  "Mode": "Fulfill",\n  "Response": "Served from ruleset.json. active_revision_id=rev-001, ruleset_version=1.0.