ption adjustment","emergency dispensation","medical dispensation"] NER CLS-PII-NAME-001 PII.PERSON_NAME 0.80 priority 5, PERSON only. Document text (exact, 4 leading '=' lines pattern as given): lines: joined with "\n". Tasks: 1. Run all 11 regex classifiers with finditer, record spans. 2. Run dictionary term matching (case-sensitive exact terms as stored; report both case-sensitive matches). 3. Run a deterministic PERSON-NER proxy (since rev-001 defines only PERSON): detect contiguous Title-case token sequences of 2-3 tokens that are labeled by a "Full Name:" style key on the same line; assign 0.80. Also report any other candidate sequences found for transparency but only emit the labeled name. 4. Filter candidates by each classifier's threshold (all candidates are at/above their own threshold). 5. Deduplicate identical spans (same start,end,classifier). 6. Deterministic overlap resolution: sort by (start asc, length desc, priority asc, confidence desc) and greedily keep non-overlapping highest-ranked spans; report any dropped spans. 7. Contextual classification check: for date matches decide DOB vs admin timestamp; for REC-/MC- etc decide log record identifier vs patient medical reference. 8. Output: final span list with start, end, matched text, category, classifier_id, confidence, priority, mask token; plus counts per category, total detections, dropped overlaps, and offsets verification (show repr of text[s:e] for each). Print everything clearly. Also print character index ruler for the document to aid verification, and confirm the address match boundaries character by character.", "user_id": "snigdhasahoo", "Timestamp": "2026-10-18T08:15:57.482316", "source": "HttpServer", "message_type": "Other", "request_id": "request-4"}
