}\b" CLS-PII-DL-001 PII.IDENTIFIER.DRIVERS_LICENSE prio3 0.85 r"\bDL-[A-Z0-9]{6,12}(?:-[A-Z]{2})?\b" CLS-PII-ADDRESS-001 PII.LOCATION.STREET_ADDRESS prio4 0.85 r"\b\d{1,5}\s+[A-Za-z0-9\s.,]+(?:Terrace|Street|St|Avenue|Ave|Road|Rd|Boulevard|Blvd|Way|Lane|Ln|Drive|Dr)(?:[A-Za-z0-9\s.,#]+)?(?:,\s+[A-Za-z\s]+,\s+[A-Z]{2}\s+\d{5}(?:-\d{4})?)?\b" Dictionary CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001 PHI.HEALTH_DATA prio3 0.85 word-bounded, case-sensitive terms: penicillin allergy, allergy, Hypertension, hypertension, prescription adjustment, emergency dispensation, medical dispensation NER CLS-PII-NAME-001 PII.PERSON_NAME prio5 0.80 PERSON only. For the PERSON NER proxy: search the FULL document with re.finditer over a pattern for Title-case name sequences of 2-4 tokens (r"\b[A-Z][a-z]+(?:\s+[A-Z][a-z]+){1,3}\b") to enumerate candidates, print ALL candidates with absolute offsets, then accept as PERSON only the candidate immediately following a "Full Name:" label (same line, absolute span). Mark the rest as rejected-by-context (not emitted) with reason. Then: dedupe identical (start,end,classifier_id). Sort candidates by (start asc, length desc, priority asc, confidence desc). Greedy non-overlap. Output final spans with absolute offsets, matched text (raw and repr), category, classifier_id, confidence, priority, suggested mask token from rev-001. Print total, per-category counts, and any dropped overlaps. Also print full document with absolute index ruler every 10 chars, and assert document_text[start:end] == matched_text for every final span. Print length of document.", "user_id": "snigdhasahoo", "Timestamp": "2026-10-18T08:16:25.795963", "source": "HttpServer", "message_type": "Other", "request_id": "request-4"}
