cedence): priority 1 = SSN, CREDIT_CARD; priority 2 = EMAIL, PHONE_NUMBER, BANK_ACCOUNT(IBAN), MEDICAL_ID; priority 3 = IP_ADDRESS, DATE_OF_BIRTH, PASSPORT, DRIVERS_LICENSE, HEALTH_DATA; priority 4 = STREET_ADDRESS; priority 5 = NAME(NER).\\nConfidence thresholds: 0.95 = SSN, CREDIT_CARD, EMAIL; 0.90 = PHONE_NUMBER, IP_ADDRESS, IBAN, MEDICAL_ID; 0.85 = DATE_OF_BIRTH, PASSPORT, DRIVERS_LICENSE, STREET_ADDRESS, HEALTH_DATA; 0.80 = NAME.\\nNamed-entity types: PERSON only (CLS-PII-NAME-001, NER).\\nDictionary terms (CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001, 7 entries): \'penicillin allergy\', \'allergy\', \'Hypertension\', \'hypertension\', \'prescription adjustment\', \'emergency dispensation\', \'medical dispensation\'.\\nHeuristics: the only heuristic-bearing classifier is CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001 (type \'dictionary_and_heuristic\'); its term list is the sole heuristic input — no separate heuristic rule objects exist in rev-001.\\nClassifier count: 13 (11 PII, 2 PHI); history shows INIT with 0 modifications; pending_admin_review is empty.\\nNote for callers: the categories tree declares types without a dedicated classifier in rev-001 (PII.IDENTIFIER.NATIONAL_ID, PII.FINANCIAL.CVV, PHI.MEDICAL_IDENTIFIER.PATIENT_ID, PHI.HEALTH_DATA.CLINICAL_NOTE); SSN is the classifier mapped to the \'SSN / National ID\' label, and PATIENT_ID/CLINICAL_NOTE are only partially covered by CLS-PHI-MED-ID-001 and CLS-PHI-CONDITION-001. Recommend citing rev-001 verbatim when reporting coverage gaps."\n}\n```'}
